digraph account_payable_process_178 {
	graph [rankdir=LR]
	START_NODE [label="" shape=circle width=0.3]
	subgraph CLUSTER_0 {
		"send to the vendor accounting department" [shape=box]
		"create a receiving report" [shape=box]
		"send to the vendor accounting department" -> "create a receiving report"
		"report errors to relevant team member" [shape=box]
		"create a receiving report" -> "report errors to relevant team member"
		"OR_SPLIT--4. Payment_T7AV" [label=O fixedsize=true shape=diamond width=0.5]
		"report errors to relevant team member" -> "OR_SPLIT--4. Payment_T7AV"
		"check dates to avoid penalty charges" [shape=box]
		"OR_SPLIT--4. Payment_T7AV" -> "check dates to avoid penalty charges"
		"enter the invoice into the accounts payable account" [shape=box]
		"OR_SPLIT--4. Payment_T7AV" -> "enter the invoice into the accounts payable account"
		"OR_JOIN--4. Payment_T7AV" [label=O fixedsize=true shape=diamond width=0.5]
		"check dates to avoid penalty charges" -> "OR_JOIN--4. Payment_T7AV"
		"enter the invoice into the accounts payable account" -> "OR_JOIN--4. Payment_T7AV"
	}
	START_NODE -> "send to the vendor accounting department"
	END_NODE [label="" shape=doublecircle width=0.2]
	"OR_JOIN--4. Payment_T7AV" -> END_NODE
	fontsize=15 label="\n\n
The following description is about the account payable process. It begins when you send to the vendor accounting department. 
Once sending to the vendor accounting department occurs, creating a receiving report should be done. 
After creating a receiving report, reporting errors to relevant team member needs to be done. 
After reporting errors to relevant team member, one or more of the following paths should be executed: checking dates to avoid penalty charges, entering the invoice into the accounts payable account. 
The process is now completed. 
"
}
